1
00:00:07,060 --> 00:00:08,675
Every note you have ever heard

2
00:00:08,715 --> 00:00:11,764
was hiding other notes inside it.

3
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:28,310
He had seven chords.

4
00:00:28,350 --> 00:00:30,848
The dark had learned all seven.

5
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:41,505
So I said his name.

6
00:00:41,545 --> 00:00:43,125
And for the first time,

7
00:00:43,165 --> 00:00:45,900
somebody in this world heard me.

8
00:00:55,060 --> 00:00:57,070
He tried to copy my voice,

9
00:00:57,110 --> 00:00:58,260
and he couldn't.

10
00:00:58,300 --> 00:01:00,932
A voice is not one note.

11
00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:11,315
So he held the lowest sound he had,

12
00:01:11,355 --> 00:01:13,268
and listened above it.

13
00:01:17,060 --> 00:01:19,095
Twice the speed, an octave.

14
00:01:19,135 --> 00:01:21,015
Three times, a fifth.

15
00:01:21,055 --> 00:01:22,692
Four, five.

16
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:36,350
He never built that chord.

17
00:01:36,390 --> 00:01:37,856
He found it.

18
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:53,540
Then the dark copied the note.

19
00:02:12,060 --> 00:02:15,292
And missed everything standing on top of it.

20
00:02:30,060 --> 00:02:31,835
It can copy what you play.

21
00:02:31,875 --> 00:02:34,844
It cannot copy what you are made of.

22
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:45,400
it cost him most of his light.
